  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1)\n\nDry conditions are expected into the middle of next week at this\ntime. Expect several continued days of similar conditions. Reduced\nafternoon dewpoints the next few days and also added in river valley\nfog. There will be the potential again tonight for some fog across\nnorthern portions of the region as well. Reduced temperatures the\nnext few nights as well as temperatures have been coming in cooler\nthan the NBM. Especially reduced temperatures across central Ohio\neast of Columbus in the typical cool spots. While a few cool spots\nelsewhere will have the potential for frost, limited most of the\nfrost mention to portions of central Ohio east of Columbus. Will add\nfrost mention in the HWO as well.",
